On Sun, May 3, 2009 at 2:14 PM, tijlan <jbotijlan@gmail.com> wrote:

> In "lo cipni cu siclu lo melbi vau .iu", does the referent of ".iu"
> includes "lo cipni"?


>From CLL 19:8:

> An attitudinal meant to cover a whole sentence can be attached to the
> preceding ``.i'', expressed or understood:
>
> 8.5)  [.i] .ia mi viska le blanu zdani
>     [belief] I see the blue house
>     I believe I see a blue house.
>
> or to an explicit ``vau'' placed at the end of a bridi.
>

So the {.iu} in your example refers to the entire bridi, and not
specifically to {lo cipni}; presumably one could love beautiful birdsong
without loving birds.

mu'o mi'e komfo,amonan

